 "segments": [
  {
   "s": 0.0,
   "e": 5.34,
   "t": "Stop me. I'm going to do it again.\" At 4 in the morning on April 24, 1973,"
  },
  {
   "s": 6.08,
   "e": 8.54,
   "t": "the desk phone rang at Santa Cruz Police Headquarters."
  },
  {
   "s": 9.3,
   "e": 14.08,
   "t": "On the line was Edmund Kemper, calling from a roadside payphone in Pueblo, Colorado,"
  },
  {
   "s": 14.48,
   "e": 18.22,
   "t": "over a thousand miles away. His voice was calm and deliberate."
  },
  {
   "s": 18.76,
   "e": 23.96,
   "t": "35. I killed my mother and her friend. And I killed those college girls. Six of them."
  },
  {
   "s": 24.82,
   "e": 29.78,
   "t": "First, Dispatch assumed it was an intoxicated prank and told him to call back later."
  },
  {
   "s": 30.54,
   "e": 36.46,
   "t": "Two hours later he called again, with words that chilled the room, 0.35, stop me, I'm"
  },
  {
   "s": 36.46,
   "e": 37.24,
   "t": "going to do it again."
  },
  {
   "s": 37.98,
   "e": 42.04,
   "t": "He didn't call to boast, he called because he was terrified that he couldn't stop"
  },
  {
   "s": 42.04,
   "e": 42.44,
   "t": "himself."
  },
  {
   "s": 43.54,
   "e": 49.4,
   "t": "When patrol cars arrived, the 6'9 giant sat peacefully in the booth, with three"
  },
  {
   "s": 49.4,
   "e": 51.58,
   "t": "rifles and hundreds of rounds in his car."
  },
  {
   "s": 51.58,
   "e": 58.02,
   "t": "His ultimate target, his mother, dead, the omnipotent fantasy dissolved into profound"
  },
  {
   "s": 58.02,
   "e": 61.22,
   "t": "emptiness, precipitating his psychological collapse."
  },
  {
   "s": 62.22,
   "e": 63.56,
   "t": "Episode 3 of Amber Eyes."
  },
  {
   "s": 64.02,
   "e": 66.14,
   "t": "Watch the full dossier via the link in our bio."
  }
 ]
}